# SQL DB Modernization Kit

This repository is the V5-reviewed SQL Server monolith-decomposition kit.

## Before editing

1. Read `README.md`, `HOW-TO-USE.md`, `REVIEW-REPORT.md`, and the nearest `AI-INSTRUCTIONS.md`.
2. Prefer canonical docs listed under “Start here” in the root README.
3. Use `AI-INSTRUCTION-INDEX.md` to find folder-specific agent instructions.
4. For DbIntelligence local setup, prefer `src-templates/DbIntelligence/scripts/` (including user-scoped Node via fnm). Prefer Codegraph install via `fnm exec --using=lts-latest -- npm i -g @colbymchenry/codegraph` when fnm is present. For YAML topology maps, prefer `tools/yaml-topology/Invoke-YamlTopologyReady.ps1` (path only).

## Safety

- Prefer additive, reversible changes; preserve ownership boundaries.
- Do not invent credentials, approvals, platform capabilities, or production values.
- Never execute destructive SQL automatically; treat `sql/` as DBA-review material.
- Keep SQL database projects and EF Core migrations projects non-overlapping.
- When behavior changes, update docs, manifests, tests, RBAC, observability, and rollback together.

## Completion

Report changed files, assumptions, validation, unresolved risks, and required approvals.
